**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery Mission**

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|---------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| **G1** | Complete Resource Delivery Mission | Ensure all requested resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` | Achieve | – |
| **G2** | Collect Resources | Perform the collection phase: determine order, request, wait, handle battery. | `;` | Perform | G1 |
| **G2.1** | Determine Storage Order | Query information about waiting time and path length to each storage to compute optimal order. | `#` | Query | G2 |
| **G2.1.1** | Calculate Waiting Time | Compute estimated waiting time for each storage. | `-` | Perform | G2.1 |
| **G2.1.2** | Calculate Path Length | Compute path length from robot to each storage. | `-` | Perform | G2.1 |
| **G2.2** | Request Resource | Send precise request message to storage. | `-` | Perform | G2 |
| **G2.3** | Wait for Retrieval | Monitor until resources are retrieved. | `-` | Perform | G2 |
| **G2.4** | Handle Low Battery (10 %) | Decide whether to continue or recharge and reassign mission. | `FALLBACK(G2.4.1,G2.4.2)` | Perform | G2 |
| **G2.4.1** | Continue Collection | Keep collecting resources. | `-` | Perform | G2.4 |
| **G2.4.2** | Recharge & Reassign | Go to recharge station and assign mission to another robot. | `-` | Perform | G2.4 |
| **G3** | Deliver Resources | Perform the delivery phase: make runs, handle battery. | `;` | Perform | G1 |
| **G3.1** | Make Delivery Runs | Transport resources from storage to specified location, possibly multiple runs. | `#` | Perform | G3 |
| **G3.1.1** | Transport Resources | Move resources to specified location. | `-` | Perform | G3.1 |
| **G3.1.2** | Drop Resources | Place resources at specified location. | `-` | Perform | G3.1 |
| **G3.2** | Handle Low Battery (30 %) | Decide whether to continue or return to checkpoint and reassign. | `FALLBACK(G3.2.1,G3.2.2)` | Perform | G3 |
| **G3.2.1** | Continue Delivery | Keep delivering resources. | `-` | Perform | G3.2 |
| **G3.2.2** | Return Resource to Checkpoint & Reassign | Return resource to checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot. | `-` | Perform | G3.2 |

---

### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|-----------|-------------------|---------------|
| **AT1** | Calculate Waiting Time | Compute estimated waiting time for each storage. | AND | Robot | 1 | Must be performed by the robot to determine the optimal order. |
| **AT2** | Calculate Path Length | Compute path length from robot to each storage. | AND | Robot | 1 | Must be performed by the robot to determine the optimal order. |
| **AT3** | Send Request Message | Send precise request message to storage. | AND | Storage | 1 | Required to initiate the resource retrieval. |
| **AT4** | Monitor Retrieval Status | Monitor until resources are retrieved. | AND | Storage | 1 | Needed to know when the robot can start delivery. |
| **AT5** | Move to Specified Location | Navigate robot to specified location for delivery. | AND | Specified Location | 1 | Required for the delivery phase. |
| **AT6** | Drop Resources | Place resources at specified location. | AND | Specified Location | 1 | Final step of the delivery. |
| **AT7** | Go to Recharge Station | Navigate robot to recharge station when battery low (10 %). | AND | Recharge Station | 1 | Needed to recharge before re‑assignment. |
| **AT8** | Notify System of Reassignment | Inform system that mission is reassigned to another robot. | AND | Robot | 1 | Required for coordination. |
| **AT9** | Return Resource to Checkpoint | Return resource to checkpoint when battery low (30 %). | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Needed to preserve resources before re‑assignment. |
| **AT10** | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | Assign remaining delivery task to another robot. | AND | Robot | 1 | Required for coordination. |
| **AT11** | Trigger Alert & Send Report | Alert sector manager if failure to return resource to checkpoint. | AND | Sector Manager | 1 | Required for fault handling. |

---

## Logical Relationships & Justifications

| Parent → Children | Relation | Runtime | Justification |
|--------------------|----------|----------|----------------|
| **G1** → G2, G3 | **AND** | `;` | Both collection and delivery must be performed; they are sequential because delivery cannot start before collection finishes. |
| **G2** → G2.1, G2.2, G2.3, G2.4 | **AND** | `;` | All sub‑goals are required for a successful collection phase; they follow one after another. |
| **G2.1** → AT1, AT2 | **AND** | `#` | Waiting time and path length can be computed in parallel; both results are needed to determine the order. |
| **G2.4** → G2.4.1, G2.4.2 | **FALLBACK** | `FALLBACK(G2.4.1,G2.4.2)` | If battery is OK, continue collection; otherwise recharge and reassign – a binary fallback. |
| **G3** → G3.1, G3.2 | **AND** | `;` | Delivery runs must be performed before handling low‑battery contingencies. |
| **G3.1** → AT5, AT6 | **AND** | `#` | Moving and dropping resources can be executed in parallel (the robot can start dropping as soon as it arrives). |
| **G3.2** → G3.2.1, G3.2.2 | **FALLBACK** | `FALLBACK(G3.2.1,G3.2.2)` | If battery is OK, continue; otherwise return to checkpoint and reassign – a binary fallback. |
| **G2.4.2** → AT7, AT8 | **AND** | `-` | Recharging and notifying the system are both required when battery is low. |
| **G3.2.2** → AT9, AT10, AT11 | **AND** | `-` | Returning to checkpoint, reassigning the task, and reporting a failure (if any) must all be performed. |

---

### Summary of Design Choices

* **Goal Types** –  
  *Achieve* for the top‑level mission because it ensures a condition (all resources delivered).  
  *Perform* for all operational goals (collection, delivery, battery handling) because they are about executing actions.  
  *Query* for “Determine Storage Order” because it requires retrieving information (waiting time, path length).

* **Runtime Annotations** –  
  *`#`* (parallel) is used where sub‑tasks can be executed concurrently (e.g., computing waiting time and path length).  
  *`;`* (sequential) is used when a strict order is required (collection before delivery, or handling battery after normal operation).  
  *`FALLBACK(...)`* is used to model binary contingencies (battery low → recharge/reassign).

* **Relations** –  
  *AND* is chosen whenever all child goals/tasks must be satisfied for the parent to succeed.  
  *OR* is not needed in this mission because there are no alternative ways to achieve a sub‑goal; all defined actions are mandatory.

* **Parallel Collection/Delivery** – The model allows multiple robots to perform “Collect Resources” and “Deliver Resources” in parallel by assigning separate instances of G2/G3 to each robot. The runtime annotation `#` at the level of G2.1 and G3.1 captures this parallelism, while the overall mission remains sequential (G2 before G3).

* **Battery Handling** – Low‑battery contingencies are explicitly modeled with fallback goals, ensuring that robots either continue or reassign/recharge as required. Failure to return a resource to a checkpoint triggers an alert task.

* **Task Locations & Robot Numbers** – All tasks specify the location where they must be executed (storage, recharge station, checkpoint, sector manager). The number of robots is set to 1 for all tasks because each action is performed by a single robot; however, the goal model allows multiple instances of the same task to be executed in parallel by different robots when needed.

This goal‑task decomposition provides a clear, justified, and executable plan for a multi‑robot resource delivery mission.
